## Time on task

Out of the sixteen finished runs of the Full
sample, the median time to completion was 26.1
minutes from start to end (interquartile range
23.0&ndash;28.1,
maximum 38.3). Responding itself took a median of
14.2 minutes, with feedback and inter-trial intervals of
the learning trials adding a fixed 6.4 minutes. The rest of
the run was spent on instructions, tutorials, the demographic form and the
debriefing.

Participants had one minute to respond on every trial.
One of
sixteen participants had at least one timed-out
learning trial, accounting for
four of 3072
learning trials in total.
Zero test
trials timed out.


